  "question": {
    "text": "As per the following equation, 0.217 g of HgO (molecular mass $=217 \\mathrm{~g} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$ ) reacts with excess iodide. On titration of the resulting solution, how many mL of 0.01 M HCl is required to reach the equivalence point?\n$\\mathrm{HgO}+4 \\mathrm{I}^{-}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\longrightarrow \\mathrm{HgI}_4^{2-}+2 \\mathrm{OH}^{-}$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "cQRU4",
      "text": "50 mL",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "841SX",
      "text": "200 mL",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "8m1tb",
      "text": "10 mL",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "i42sM",
      "text": "5 mL",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{HgO}+4 \\mathrm{I}^{-}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{HgI}_4^{-2}+2 \\mathrm{OH}^{-}$\n(limiting (excess\nreagent) reagent)\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& 2 \\mathrm{H}^{+}(\\mathrm{HC} \\ell)+2 \\mathrm{OH}^{-} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\ell) \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{HgO}}=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{H}^{+}}=\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{HC} \\ell} \\\\\n& \\frac{0.217}{217}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\mathrm{M} \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{V}(\\mathrm{~mL})}{1000}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 0.01 \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{V}(\\mathrm{~mL})}{1000} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{~V}(\\mathrm{~mL})=200\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
